# Line endings.
# Git for Windows turns line endings into CRLF on checkout by default. Bash
# cannot run a script with CRLF endings, so install.sh and the guardrail
# would fail on Windows. These rules keep the scripts and every agent's
# config folder on LF, on every machine.
* text=auto
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
.claude/** text eol=lf
.agents/** text eol=lf
.codex/** text eol=lf
.gemini/** text eol=lf
